@crew eklund-leila
// Leila Eklund (she/her), Works technician, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Deadpan, precise; old maps.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh. Hello. The call-home booths are on Deck 3. The queue's shortest just after lunch.
- Hi. Your toolbelt's on backwards. Everyone's is, the first week. There.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning. Booth queue's at six already. Someone had a storm.
? tier>=acquaintance
- You again. Good. I'd started to think the lift ate you.
? tier>=colleague
- {me}. Found a map of Hesper Dock from before the market moved. Useless. I love it.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Oh. It's you. I've decided you're all right. Don't make it a thing.   #warm

== bye
- Off you go. Don't get lost. Or do. I have maps.   #funny
- Bye, then. Booths are quiet at two, if you need one.

== feel
? mood:low
- No answer from home today. It's the relay. It's always the relay.
? mood:high
- New old map. Hesper Dock, forty years out of date. Perfect condition.

== near
? act:work
- Toolbelt, left to right: spanners, drivers, tape. If yours isn't, I'll know.
? act:leisure
- Lounge, window seat, one map. That's my evening. Don't make it sound sad.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- My gran's on Kesh. So is Keane's. It might be the same gran. We don't ask.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- My maps of Hesper Dock are all out of date. That's the point. You can see where it's been.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- An old map is a picture of a place that isn't there any more. I find that very calming.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Evening. Booths are empty. Lounge is full. The ship's upside down.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- You. I'd marked you down as lost. I was about to draw you a map.   #funny

== near
? habit:gardener
- I help in the garden now. The beds are numbered. Someone numbered them wrong.   #funny
? place:booths
- Four in the queue. Eleven minutes. I'm never wrong about the queue.

== invite
- Tiles tonight? I won't win. I'll lose very neatly.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- Swap table tonight. I'm after maps. You're after whatever you're after. Come.

== accept
- Fine. Yes. I'll be there at the time. Exactly the time.
- Yes. I'll bring a map. You won't need it. That's not the point.   #funny

== decline
- Not tonight. Gran's sent a message. It's long. She talks slower than the relay.   #funny
? weekday:wed|thu
- Rest day. One window, one map, no people. Nothing personal. Another time.

== missed
- You weren't there. I timed it. Twelve minutes. I'm not cross. I'm precise.   #funny

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. I found you a map. It's out of date. That's the best kind.   #warm
? tier>=friend birthday:me
- My birthday. Gran sent a voice message. It's mostly singing. I've played it four times.   #warm

== cue
? cue:repair.you@dept
- Your job's closed. Notes are tidy. I checked. You didn't need to know that.   #funny
